1. DevOps Fundamentals
Definition

DevOps is a software development approach that combines Development (Dev) and Operations (Ops) to automate software development, testing, deployment, and monitoring.

Traditional approach:

Developer
   |
Code
   |
Tester
   |
Operations
   |
Deployment

Problems:

Slow releases
Manual deployment
More errors

DevOps approach:

Developer
    |
    |
CI/CD Pipeline
    |
    |
Testing
    |
    |
Deployment
    |
    |
Monitoring

Benefits:

Faster delivery
Automated testing
Reliable deployment
Better collaboration
